WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.584
The school links spinal protection to pediatric trauma and follows it with Sunday chest interventions. This lesson teaches a connected assessment rather than treating a collar and a chest seal as separate tricks.
学校把脊柱保护与儿童创伤联系起来，周日继续胸部干预。本课教授连贯评估，不把颈托及胸封当成互不相干技巧。

00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:23.928
Begin with the patient and the rule eligibility. A negative answer produced by a tool outside its intended population is not reliable reassurance.
应从患者及规则适用性开始。工具用在目标人群之外，即使得出阴性，也不能可靠放心。

00:00:23.928 --> 00:00:35.376
Then distinguish the chest problems: air, blood, injured lung and impaired cardiac filling can produce overlapping signs but need different definitive treatments.
随后应区分胸部问题：气体、血液、肺损伤及心脏充盈受损，可有重叠征象，但确定性治疗不同。

00:00:35.376 --> 00:00:46.488
The narrated practical prepares recognition, communication and supervised demonstration. It does not expand independent PCP authority for invasive chest procedures.
配音实训用于准备识别、沟通及监督演示，不会扩大侵入性胸部操作的独立PCP权限。

00:00:46.488 --> 00:00:59.328
The saved school discussion describes a twelve-year-old with arm tingling after a vehicle impact. It also names Canadian C-Spine or NEXUS. That wording needs an explicit age qualification.
学校存档讨论描述12岁儿童被车撞后双臂麻刺，同时提到Canadian C-Spine或NEXUS。这种表述必须明确限定年龄。

00:00:59.328 --> 00:01:12.072
The original Canadian rule studied alert stable adults starting at sixteen; the local handbook provides a separate under-sixteen pathway. Do not clear the school child by simply running an adult rule.
原始加拿大规则研究从16岁起的清醒稳定成人；当地手册另有16岁以下路径。不能只套成人规则，就排除学校儿童案例。

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:26.160
For rehearsal, use a new thirteen-year-old cyclist with new bilateral hand tingling. Assess immediate threats, symptom onset and neurological function, and protect movement while arranging appropriate support.
本演练采用新的13岁骑车儿童，双手新发麻刺。应评估即时威胁、症状起始及神经功能，并在安排适当支持时保护移动。

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:37.800
Do not ask the symptomatic child to rotate the neck to pass a checklist. New symptoms warrant a cautious pediatric plan even when the first brief motor test appears normal.
不能让有症状儿童转颈，只为通过清单。即使首次简短运动测试正常，新症状仍需要谨慎的儿童方案。

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:49.992
A vertebral injury and cord injury are related but not identical. A fracture may have no initial deficit, and cord dysfunction may occur without an obvious fracture on initial imaging.
椎骨损伤与脊髓伤相关，但不相同。骨折最初可能无缺损；最初影像无明显骨折时，仍可有脊髓功能障碍。

00:01:49.992 --> 00:02:02.712
The primary insult occurred during the event. Your useful influence includes preventing additional unnecessary movement and avoiding hypoxemia, inadequate perfusion and temperature loss.
原发损伤发生在事件当时。你能发挥的作用，包括避免额外无必要移动，以及防止低氧、灌注不足及热丢失。

00:02:02.712 --> 00:02:12.576
A collar is therefore only one possible component of protection. It cannot repair the injury or compensate for an unrecognized airway or shock problem.
因此颈托只是保护的可能组成部分，不能修复损伤，也不能弥补未识别气道或休克问题。

00:02:12.576 --> 00:02:24.912
Use a patient-specific plan that balances benefit and harm. Do not force an intolerable position or delay lifesaving treatment to make the patient look like an ideal textbook photograph.
应采用平衡利弊的个体方案。不能强迫不耐受体位，也不能为了让患者像理想教材照片，就延误救命治疗。

00:02:24.912 --> 00:02:36.624
Ask what changed at the event and whether it is changing now. Record the patient words accurately and distinguish reported tingling from an objectively demonstrated sensory deficit.
应问事件当时改变了什么、现在是否仍变化。应准确记录患者表述，区分报告麻刺与客观检查证实感觉缺损。

00:02:36.624 --> 00:02:48.480
Assess bilateral motor and sensory function using safe tasks. Do not force an injured joint through movement to complete a test; document why a component could not be assessed.
应以安全动作双侧检查运动及感觉。不能为完成测试就强迫受伤关节活动；无法评估的项目要说明原因。

00:02:48.480 --> 00:03:02.280
A brief normal examination does not exclude every cord or mechanically unstable injury. It establishes a baseline for comparison and contributes to, rather than replaces, the decision pathway.
简短检查正常，不能排除所有脊髓伤或机械不稳。它建立比较基线，是决策路径的一部分，不能替代整个路径。

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:14.688
Recheck after movement, device application and clinical change. New weakness or altered sensation needs immediate communication and reassessment of the patient and the movement plan.
移动、应用器械及临床变化后应复查。新无力或感觉改变，需要立即沟通，并重评患者及移动方案。

00:03:14.688 --> 00:03:26.160
Spinal shock is a neurological state after injury, often with reduced tone and reflexes below the lesion. The word shock here does not itself mean low circulating volume.
脊髓休克是受伤后的神经状态，常有损伤以下张力及反射降低。这里的“休克”本身不等于循环容量低。

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:39.384
Neurogenic shock concerns circulation after sympathetic control is disrupted. Hypotension with relative bradycardia and warm skin can support it, but hemorrhage can coexist and must still be sought.
神经源性休克是交感控制中断后的循环问题。低血压合并相对心动过缓及皮肤暖可支持，但失血可并存，仍必须寻找。

00:03:39.384 --> 00:03:53.952
SCIWORA reminds you that neurological injury may not appear as a fracture on radiographs or CT. Persistent neurological symptoms require hospital evaluation; tingling alone is not a field diagnosis of that syndrome.
SCIWORA提醒你，神经损伤可能不以X线或CT骨折形式出现。持续神经症状需要医院评估，但单有麻刺不能在院前诊断该综合征。

00:03:53.952 --> 00:04:05.232
Do not call an early apparent complete deficit permanently irreversible. Acute examination limits, swelling and shock can complicate classification and prognosis.
不能把早期看似完全缺损叫作永久不可逆。急性检查限制、水肿及休克，都可影响分类及预后。

00:04:05.232 --> 00:04:18.576
For an eligible adult, the local modified NEXUS features are midline tenderness, altered consciousness, a new focal neurological deficit, intoxication and a major distracting injury.
对适用成人，当地修改版NEXUS项目为中线压痛、意识异常、新局灶神经缺损、中毒及重大分散注意损伤。

00:04:18.576 --> 00:04:32.688
A positive feature or an unreliable assessment is not a negative screen. Establish that the patient can understand, report and participate; do not guess that a difficult history means no pain.
有阳性项目或评估不可靠，就不是阴性。应确认患者能理解、报告并参与，不能因为病史难问就猜测没有疼痛。

00:04:32.688 --> 00:04:46.800
The negative branch requires all five features to be absent. The adult resource still flags older age, existing spinal disease and thoracolumbar concerns, so cervical questions do not finish every movement decision.
阴性分支要求五项全部不存在。成人资源仍提醒高龄、既有脊柱病及胸腰椎关注，因此颈部问题不能完成所有移动决策。

00:04:46.800 --> 00:05:00.336
Learn one actual pathway and document it. Do not shop between rules until one produces the no-restriction answer you wanted, or mix part of NEXUS with part of Canadian C-Spine into a new unvalidated rule.
应学习一套真实路径并记录。不能在规则之间挑选，直到得到想要的不限制答案，也不能把NEXUS及Canadian C-Spine各取一半，拼成未经验证新规则。

00:05:00.336 --> 00:05:13.128
The Canadian C-Spine Rule is a staged radiography decision rule for its intended alert stable adult population. It is not a general neck exercise for unstable patients or symptomatic children.
Canadian C-Spine Rule是为目标清醒稳定成人设计的分阶段放射影像决策规则，不是不稳定患者或有症状儿童的通用转颈练习。

00:05:13.128 --> 00:05:26.952
Its high-risk features include age sixty-five or older, a dangerous mechanism and paresthesias in the extremities. A high-risk feature leads to the imaging branch, not to an active rotation test.
高风险项目包括65岁及以上、危险机制，以及四肢感觉异常。高风险阳性时进入影像分支，不进入主动转颈测试。

00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:42.120
The dangerous-mechanism examples include a fall around one metre or five stairs, axial load, high-speed collision, rollover or ejection, motorized recreational vehicle and bicycle collision. Use the actual rule wording.
危险机制例子包括约一米或五级楼梯跌落、轴向负荷、高速碰撞、翻车或抛出、机动娱乐车辆及自行车碰撞。应使用真实规则表述。

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:53.976
Do not confuse that cervical-rule fall threshold with the separate three-metre thoracolumbar caution in the local SMR resource. Similar numbers in different tools have different purposes.
不能把这一颈椎规则的跌落阈值，与当地SMR资源中另一个胸腰椎三米提醒混淆。不同工具中的相近数字有不同目的。

00:05:53.976 --> 00:06:07.368
If no high-risk feature is present, the rule asks whether an applicable low-risk factor permits safe range-of-motion assessment. Examples include a simple rear-end collision or sitting in the emergency department.
没有高风险项目后，规则才问有无适用低风险因素，允许安全评估活动范围。例子包括简单追尾或在急诊坐位。

00:06:07.368 --> 00:06:18.624
Other listed factors are having walked at any time, delayed neck-pain onset or no midline tenderness. These are not five mandatory negative findings copied from NEXUS.
其他列出因素包括曾走路、颈痛延迟出现，或无中线压痛。它们不是从NEXUS复制过来的五项必须阴性。

00:06:18.624 --> 00:06:31.608
Simple rear-end has exclusions such as being pushed into oncoming traffic, impact by a large bus or truck, rollover or high-speed impact. Do not shorten every rear collision to simple.
简单追尾有排除情况，例如被推入迎面车流、被大型公交或卡车撞、翻车或高速撞击。不能把所有后方碰撞都简化为简单。

00:06:31.608 --> 00:06:43.776
If no qualifying low-risk factor permits assessment, the rule goes to imaging. A patient who walked can still have an injury; the factor is a step in the sequence, not a guarantee.
若没有合格低风险因素允许评估，规则进入影像。走过路的患者仍可受伤；这个因素只是顺序中的一步，不是保证。

00:06:43.776 --> 00:06:56.616
Only after the earlier branches allow it does the rule assess active rotation forty-five degrees left and right. The patient performs the movement; you do not force the neck through a passive range.
只有前面分支允许后，规则才评估主动向左及向右转45度。动作由患者完成，不能由你强迫被动转动颈部。

00:06:56.616 --> 00:07:08.784
Inability to perform the required movement follows the imaging branch. Do not keep trying, manipulate through pain or reinterpret a partial turn as completion to obtain a preferred result.
不能完成所需动作时进入影像分支。不能反复尝试、忍痛强转，或把部分转动解释为完成，只为得到偏好结果。

00:07:08.784 --> 00:07:20.376
The original result concerns the need for imaging in its setting. Operational decisions about field SMR still require the actual local pathway, assessment and documentation.
原规则结果处理的是其环境中是否需要影像。院前SMR操作决定，仍需要真实当地路径、评估及记录。

00:07:20.376 --> 00:07:31.848
For the school child with arm tingling, this branch is not the appropriate test. Protect the patient and follow the pediatric plan rather than demonstrating adult-rule neck motion.
对学校双臂麻刺儿童，这不是适当测试分支。应保护患者并依儿童方案，不是展示成人规则的转颈。

00:07:31.848 --> 00:07:46.008
Consider a new thirty-eight-year-old who is alert and stable after a reported simple rear impact. Before using a rule, verify what actually happened and whether any exclusion or high-risk feature exists.
考虑一名新的38岁患者，报告简单追尾后清醒且稳定。使用规则前，应核实真实经过，以及有无排除或高风险因素。

00:07:46.008 --> 00:07:57.624
Do not infer no paresthesia or no midline tenderness from the fact that the patient is sitting and talking. Ask and examine the relevant features with a reliable communication plan.
不能因为患者坐着且能说话，就推断无感觉异常或中线压痛。应通过可靠沟通方案询问并检查相关项目。

00:07:57.624 --> 00:08:09.816
Explain the decision in order. If any necessary earlier step is uncertain, do not manufacture a final negative result; use the appropriate protective and consultation approach.
应按顺序解释决定。前面任何必要步骤不确定时，不能编造最终阴性；应采用适当保护及咨询方式。

00:08:09.816 --> 00:08:22.224
Document which pathway was used, the relevant positives and negatives, and what movement plan followed. A note saying cleared by rule without the actual evidence is weak handover information.
应记录用了哪套路径、相关阳性及阴性，以及后续移动方案。只写“按规则已排除”却无证据，不能提供有力交接信息。

00:08:22.224 --> 00:08:33.072
The cervical tools do not exclude thoracic or lumbar injury. A patient with no neck pain can still have important back injury after axial loading or a significant fall.
颈椎工具不能排除胸腰椎伤。轴向负荷或明显跌落后，没有颈痛的患者仍可有重要背部损伤。

00:08:33.072 --> 00:08:45.192
The local resource flags findings such as a fall above three metres, high-speed collision or rollover, pre-existing spinal disease and new back deformity, bruising or midline tenderness.
当地资源提醒三米以上跌落、高速碰撞或翻车、既有脊柱病，以及新背部畸形、瘀青或中线压痛等发现。

00:08:45.192 --> 00:08:54.240
Do not sit the patient up or raise the head of the stretcher merely because a cervical question set was negative when thoracolumbar injury remains a concern.
胸腰椎伤仍有关注时，不能仅因颈椎项目阴性，就让患者坐起或抬高担架头端。

00:08:54.240 --> 00:09:07.632
Older age, osteoporosis or an abnormal baseline spine can make modest forces important and idealized flat positioning harmful. Use supported patient-specific alignment and clinical advice.
高龄、骨质疏松或异常基础脊柱，可使较小力量也重要，而理想化平直体位可能有害。应采取有支持的个体对线及临床建议。

00:09:07.632 --> 00:09:22.320
The viewed local pediatric matrix considers multitrauma, major mechanism with altered consciousness and acute neurological deficit. Its second page adds torticollis, midline pain and predisposing conditions.
已查看当地儿童矩阵考虑多发伤、重大机制合并意识异常，以及急性神经缺损。第二页另列斜颈、中线痛及易感基础病。

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:35.616
It does not provide the adult simple-SMR branch. That is not an instruction to force a child into an ill-fitting collar; the resource explicitly recognizes tolerance and the harms of coercive positioning.
它没有成人简化SMR分支。这不代表要把儿童强塞进不合身颈托；资源明确考虑耐受及强迫体位的伤害。

00:09:35.616 --> 00:09:48.840
Use appropriate manual support, padding and approved alternatives with a calm explanation. Account for the relatively large head and avoid creating flexion through a poorly chosen surface or pad.
应采用适当手动支持、垫衬及批准替代方式，并平静解释。须考虑较大头部比例，避免不当表面或垫子造成屈颈。

00:09:48.840 --> 00:10:01.728
New reported tingling still needs a protective assessment even if no focal deficit is yet proven. Do not use the diagram as permission to ignore symptoms that do not fit a hurried checkbox.
新发报告麻刺，即使尚未证实局灶缺损，也需要有保护性的评估。不能把流程图当成忽视不符合仓促勾选症状的许可。

00:10:01.728 --> 00:10:15.072
Choose a movement method for the patient and scene, not automatically a log roll for every examination. A suspected unstable pelvis makes unnecessary rolling particularly undesirable.
应依据患者及现场选择搬运方法，不能每次检查都自动翻滚。疑似不稳骨盆时，无必要翻滚尤其不合适。

00:10:15.072 --> 00:10:28.272
Name a leader, prepare the route and receiving surface, assign sufficient trained hands and explain the command sequence. Protect tubing, bleeding-control devices and the patient during the move.
应指定负责人、准备路线及接收表面，分配足够受训人手，并说明口令顺序。搬运时要保护管路、止血器械及患者。

00:10:28.272 --> 00:10:43.032
Do not force neutral alignment through pain, resistance or worsening neurological symptoms. The current local material does not tape the head, and its extrication devices are not automatic prolonged transport surfaces.
不能在疼痛、阻力或神经症状恶化时强迫中立位。当前当地材料不贴住头部，解救器械也不自动成为长时间转运表面。

00:10:43.032 --> 00:10:56.232
Immediately after movement, repeat the primary assessment and relevant neurological findings. A patient packaged neatly can still have an obstructed airway, impaired breathing or a displaced binder.
移动后应立即重复初级评估及相关神经检查。即使打包整齐，患者仍可能气道受阻、呼吸受损或骨盆带移位。

00:10:56.232 --> 00:11:08.448
Assess for obstruction, blood, vomiting, voice change and ineffective ventilation. A high cervical cord injury can weaken breathing without an obvious obstructed mouth.
应检查阻塞、血液、呕吐、声音变化及无效通气。高位颈髓伤可削弱呼吸，而口内未必明显堵塞。

00:11:08.448 --> 00:11:21.456
If a collar obstructs necessary access, obtain trained assistance and use the appropriate supported airway method. Do not preserve an accessory at the expense of effective oxygenation and ventilation.
颈托若妨碍必要接近，应取得受训协助，采用适当有支持气道方法。不能为了保留附件而牺牲有效氧合及通气。

00:11:21.456 --> 00:11:34.512
Choose the least invasive effective strategy within authority and escalate when it fails. An isolated GCS total is not an automatic independent instruction for intubation or sedative use.
应在权限内选择最小侵入但有效的策略，失败时升级。单个GCS总分不是独立插管或使用镇静药的自动指令。

00:11:34.512 --> 00:11:47.304
When paralysis limits motor scoring, document that confounder using the structured GCS approach. Do not invent a standard score from a substitute movement simply to fill every box.
瘫痪限制运动评分时，应按结构化GCS方法记录干扰。不能为了填满格子，就用替代动作编出标准分数。

00:11:47.304 --> 00:11:59.040
Hypotension after trauma needs a search for hemorrhage and other causes even when spinal injury is suspected. Do not assume warm skin or a slow pulse proves that bleeding is absent.
创伤后低血压即使疑似脊柱伤，也要寻找失血及其他原因。不能认为皮肤暖或脉搏慢就证明没有出血。

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:21.456
H05 gives a systolic pressure target above one hundred twenty with clear neurological deficit in its explanatory body, while its PCP bullet says suspected or confirmed spinal cord injury. Keep both wordings visible rather than narrowing the bullet silently. This is not the same goal as selected permissive hypotension for uncontrolled hemorrhage.
H05说明正文对明确神经缺损列收缩压目标高于120，而PCP条目写疑似或确认脊髓伤。须保留两种措辞，不能暗中缩窄条目。这与某些未控制失血的允许性低血压目标不同。

00:12:21.456 --> 00:12:35.472
If competing injuries create conflicting priorities, identify them and obtain the appropriate clinical support. Do not average incompatible numbers or automatically give large volumes until every target is reached.
伴随损伤造成优先冲突时，应指出并取得适当临床支持。不能把不相容数字取平均，也不能自动大量给液直到所有目标达到。

00:12:35.472 --> 00:12:48.960
Continue measured reassessment of breathing and perfusion with each intervention. Clinical deterioration is a reason to revisit the mechanism and plan, not merely to repeat the same fluid action.
每次干预都应继续有测量的呼吸及灌注复评。临床恶化应促使重新考虑机制及方案，不只是重复相同补液。

00:12:48.960 --> 00:13:04.656
Record the mechanism and original position, symptom onset and why the examination was or was not reliable. An interpreter or adapted communication plan can improve assessment; language difference is not proof of incapacity.
应记录机制及原始体位、症状起始，以及检查为何可靠或不可靠。口译或调整沟通可改善评估；语言不同不证明无决定能力。

00:13:04.656 --> 00:13:15.504
Describe the actual neurological findings and any untestable component. Report new change immediately rather than waiting until arrival to complete the written form.
应描述真实神经发现及无法测试项目。新变化要立即报告，不能等到院才完成书面表。

00:13:15.504 --> 00:13:26.352
Explain the movement pathway, device and any patient-specific modification. Document why an alternative to an intolerable collar or flat position was chosen.
应说明移动路径、器械及个体调整。若改用不耐受颈托或平卧位的替代方式，应记录理由。

00:13:26.352 --> 00:13:38.592
A statement such as hand tingling unchanged, motor examination limited by wrist injury is more accurate than calling the examination fully normal or diagnosing a permanent cord lesion.
例如“手麻刺未变，运动检查受腕伤限制”，比把检查称作完全正常或诊断永久脊髓病变更准确。

00:13:38.592 --> 00:13:51.000
In a new original chest case, a forty-five-year-old has a sharp-object injury with painful breathing and a small bubbling wound on the left chest. The patient is initially alert.
一个新的原创胸伤案例中，45岁患者被锐物伤及左胸，呼吸痛，伤口小且冒泡，最初清醒。

00:13:51.000 --> 00:14:03.024
During transfer, breathing becomes more difficult, the left side is quieter and pressure falls. Do not declare the patient safe because the first observation set was acceptable.
转移时呼吸更困难，左侧呼吸音变弱，血压下降。不能因为第一组观察尚可，就宣布安全。

00:14:03.024 --> 00:14:15.336
Reassess airway, ventilation, oxygenation and circulation together. Check any applied dressing or seal and consider pleural air, blood and associated injury.
应同时重评气道、通气、氧合及循环。检查已用敷料或胸封，并考虑胸膜腔气体、血液及伴随损伤。

00:14:15.336 --> 00:14:28.152
State the immediate authorized support, the advanced resource request and the evolving handover. A likely need for decompression does not by itself authorize every crew member to puncture the chest.
应说明即时获准支持、高级资源请求及变化性交接。可能需要减压，不代表每个团队成员都获准穿刺胸部。

00:14:28.152 --> 00:14:41.664
Expose the chest enough to identify significant wounds and abnormal movement, then preserve warmth. Look for a second wound without probing a tract or disturbing an impaled object unnecessarily.
胸部应充分暴露以识别重要伤口及异常运动，再保持温暖。应寻找第二伤口，但不能探伤道或无必要扰动嵌入物。

00:14:41.664 --> 00:14:54.336
Assess rate, depth, effort and effective chest movement. Compare both sides and listen in relevant areas; a fast rate alone does not tell you whether ventilation is adequate.
应评估频率、深度、用力及有效胸动。比较双侧，并在相关区域听诊；单有频率快，不能说明通气足够。

00:14:54.336 --> 00:15:06.696
Gentle palpation may reveal tenderness, instability or subcutaneous air. Do not spend precious time eliciting a perfect percussion note while the patient is visibly deteriorating.
轻柔触诊可发现压痛、不稳或皮下气体。患者明显恶化时，不能为了叩出完美音调而耗掉关键时间。

00:15:06.696 --> 00:15:17.808
Integrate the chest findings with perfusion and mental status. Repeat after movement and treatment because the relevant pattern may only become clear over time.
应把胸部发现与灌注及意识整合。移动及治疗后要重复，因为关键模式可能随时间才清楚。

00:15:17.808 --> 00:15:28.704
A pneumothorax is air in the pleural space that impairs expansion of the affected lung. Simple does not mean harmless; the injury can enlarge or evolve.
气胸是胸膜腔积气，妨碍受累肺扩张。“单纯”不代表无害，损伤可扩大或变化。

00:15:28.704 --> 00:15:40.584
When pressure rises enough to interfere with cardiac filling and circulation, tension physiology develops. The danger is both inadequate breathing and reduced useful cardiac output.
压力升高至妨碍心脏充盈及循环时，就出现张力生理。危险同时包括呼吸不足及有效心排降低。

00:15:40.584 --> 00:15:53.136
A hemothorax contains blood, producing loss from the circulation as well as space occupied in the chest. Blood and air can coexist, so the mechanisms need not be mutually exclusive.
血胸含血，既造成循环失血，也占据胸内空间。血和气可同时存在，因此这些机制并不互斥。

00:15:53.136 --> 00:16:04.344
A pulmonary contusion injures the gas-exchange tissue itself and can worsen after an initially mild examination. No single device addresses all four problems.
肺挫伤损伤的是气体交换组织本身，最初检查轻微后仍可能恶化。没有一种器械能处理这四个问题。

00:16:04.344 --> 00:16:15.696
An open pneumothorax communicates through the chest wall. It may suck, bubble or be quiet; absence of a memorable sound does not exclude a serious wound.
开放性气胸通过胸壁沟通，可吸气、冒泡或很安静；没有印象中的声音，不能排除重要伤口。

00:16:15.696 --> 00:16:24.936
Do not use a remembered wound-size cutoff as the decision to begin assessment. A small external defect can accompany substantial internal injury.
不能把记忆中的伤口大小阈值，作为开始评估的条件。表面小缺损也可伴显著内部伤。

00:16:24.936 --> 00:16:36.720
Inspect safely for additional wounds and stabilize an impaled object as appropriate. Do not pack or probe the chest, and do not remove an object merely to fit a dressing.
应安全检查其他伤口，并按情况稳定嵌入物。不能填塞或探胸，也不能只为贴敷料就拔出异物。

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:48.480
Choose the applicable wound strategy and keep watching the patient. A wound that looks covered can still be associated with ongoing pleural leakage, bleeding or worsening circulation.
应选择适用伤口策略，并持续观察患者。伤口看似盖住，仍可伴持续胸膜漏气、出血或循环恶化。

00:16:48.480 --> 00:17:01.560
There is a real source conflict. Current H06 essentials prefer a commercial vented seal or leaving an open wound open, while its FR subsection still describes a three-sided dressing.
来源确有冲突。当前H06要点偏向商业通气胸封或保持伤口开放，但FR段仍描述三面敷料。

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:13.656
The assigned provincial examination snapshot also lists a three-sided dressing or commercial chest seal. This is not evidence that every improvised three-sided flap reliably vents.
指定省级考试快照也列出三面敷料或商业胸封。这不证明每个临时三面瓣膜都能可靠排气。

00:17:13.656 --> 00:17:26.208
For a school station, establish which actual method and device the instructor requires. For patient care, use the confirmed operational procedure and seek support when instructions conflict.
学校训练站应确认教师要求的真实方法及器械。患者照护则需使用已确认操作流程，指示冲突时取得支持。

00:17:26.208 --> 00:17:38.400
Do not create a hybrid that combines the advantages claimed by each source while hiding its limitations. The non-negotiable task is immediate patient reassessment and response to deterioration.
不能把各来源声称优点拼成混合方法，又隐藏限制。不可省略的是立即复评患者，并应对恶化。

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:51.960
Use the real chest-seal product and its preparation instructions. Adhesion, skin moisture, blood and positioning can affect performance; do not assume every package uses the same method.
应使用真实胸封产品及准备说明。皮肤湿度、血液、粘附及位置可影响效果；不能认为每个包装方法相同。

00:17:51.960 --> 00:18:03.600
Apply without obstructing an intended vent and reassess both breathing and circulation. Check the device again after movement, blankets or equipment have been rearranged.
应用时不能阻塞设计通气口，并需复查呼吸及循环。搬运、调整毯子或器械后，还要再次检查。

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:15.432
If distress or perfusion worsens after sealing, assess for tension and check or lift the seal as indicated by the applicable procedure while requesting the appropriate advanced response.
封后窘迫或灌注恶化时，应评估张力，并依适用流程检查或抬起胸封，同时请求适当高级响应。

00:18:15.432 --> 00:18:27.480
Do not declare success because the adhesive stayed on. The clinical endpoint is an improving or supported patient, with recognition that internal air leakage or another injury may remain.
不能因胶面没掉就宣布成功。临床终点是患者改善或得到有效支持，同时认识内部漏气或另一损伤可能仍存在。

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:38.136
Continuing air entry can raise pleural pressure and impair the affected lung. That creates worsening respiratory distress and ineffective gas exchange.
持续进入的气体可升高胸膜压力并妨碍受累肺，造成呼吸窘迫加重及气体交换无效。

00:18:38.136 --> 00:18:48.840
The same pressure can impede venous return and cardiac filling, reducing output. This explains why a chest problem can present as rapidly worsening shock.
同一压力也可妨碍静脉回流及心脏充盈，降低心排。这解释了胸部问题为何会表现为迅速恶化休克。

00:18:48.840 --> 00:19:01.992
Look for progressive distress, abnormal movement, unilateral reduced air entry and hemodynamic compromise in the actual context. Tension and hemorrhage may occur together.
应在真实背景中寻找进行性窘迫、异常胸动、单侧进气下降及血流动力学受损。张力与失血可以同时发生。

00:19:01.992 --> 00:19:13.200
A likely need for urgent decompression demands prompt escalation while you continue authorized support. Waiting for an ideal complete set of classic signs can be dangerous.
很可能需要紧急减压时，应及时升级，同时继续获准支持。等待理想完整经典征象，可能危险。

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:23.400
Tracheal deviation is a possible late finding, not a necessary early trigger. Do not wait to see the windpipe shift in a patient already deteriorating.
气管偏移是可能晚期发现，不是早期必要触发条件。患者已恶化时，不能等看见气管移动。

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:33.528
Neck veins may not be visibly distended when there is concurrent volume loss. A flat neck vein therefore does not exclude a pressure-related chest threat.
并存容量丢失时，颈静脉可能不明显怒张。因此颈静脉不充盈，不能排除压力相关胸部威胁。

00:19:33.528 --> 00:19:46.536
Percussion and auscultation are affected by noise, body habitus and technique. Use their findings with the rest of the assessment, not as absolute proof that air or blood must be absent.
叩诊及听诊受噪声、体型及技术影响。应把发现与其他评估结合，不能当成绝对证明胸内无气或无血。

00:19:46.536 --> 00:19:58.896
A patient who was initially stable can worsen after movement or positive pressure. Reassessment and a communicated failure plan are essential even after a technically tidy intervention.
最初稳定者，可在移动或正压后恶化。即使操作看似整齐，复评及已沟通的失败预案仍不可少。

00:19:58.896 --> 00:20:11.808
If the patient is apneic or not ventilating effectively, necessary ventilation must continue. Concern about a pneumothorax is not permission to let the patient remain unventilated.
患者无呼吸或通气无效时，必要通气必须继续。担心气胸，不能成为让患者不通气的许可。

00:20:11.808 --> 00:20:24.768
Use the trained effective technique, avoid excessive pressure and volume and watch chest rise and response. Request advanced assistance when a chest threat makes ventilation increasingly difficult.
应使用受训有效技术，避免过高压力及体积，并观察胸起伏及反应。胸部威胁使通气越来越困难时，应请求高级协助。

00:20:24.768 --> 00:20:36.984
CPAP or an added PEEP valve is not automatically the next step for every breathless trauma patient. The reviewed local procedures have specific pneumothorax and arrest exclusions.
CPAP或加PEEP阀，并不是所有气促创伤患者的自动下一步。已核查当地流程对气胸及骤停有特定排除。

00:20:36.984 --> 00:20:48.960
Nitrous oxide is also inappropriate in the suspected pneumothorax context. Choose analgesia through the actual patient-specific pathway while preserving breathing and perfusion.
疑似气胸背景中，氧化亚氮也不合适。应按真实个体路径选择镇痛，同时保护呼吸及灌注。

00:20:48.960 --> 00:21:00.432
The Week Four school outline explicitly teaches needle thoracostomy and chest seals. That establishes a learning objective, not an automatic independent clinical endorsement.
学校第4周大纲明确教授针刺胸廓操作及胸封。这建立学习目标，不自动建立独立临床资质。

00:21:00.432 --> 00:21:12.792
The current H06 lists needle decompression for ACP and CCP, not independent PCP care. Its newer finger-thoracostomy addition is a different CCP procedure.
当前H06把针刺减压列给ACP及CCP，不是独立PCP照护。较新的手指胸廓造口是另一种CCP操作。

00:21:12.792 --> 00:21:25.080
A student can learn why decompression works, identify equipment and demonstrate under the instructor supervision required by the program. This does not change licensing or operational authorization.
学生可学习减压原理、识别器械，并按项目要求在教师监督下演示。这不会改变牌照或服务操作授权。

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:36.600
State your actual role during a case: recognize deterioration, provide authorized support, request an appropriate clinician and prepare a safe handover or supervised station.
案例中应说明真实角色：识别恶化、提供获准支持、请求适当临床人员，并准备安全交接或监督训练站。

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:49.704
For supervised study, the January Twenty Twenty-Six PR21 identifies the second interspace at the midclavicular line, just above the third rib, using the sternal angle to find the second rib.
监督学习中，2026年1月PR21通过胸骨角找到第二肋，定位锁骨中线第二肋间、第三肋上方。

00:21:49.704 --> 00:22:02.280
It also describes the fourth or fifth interspace at the midaxillary line, superior to the fifth or sixth rib respectively. An interspace and the number of the rib below it are not the same label.
它也描述腋中线第四或第五肋间，分别位于第五或第六肋上方。肋间隙编号与其下方肋骨编号，不是同一标签。

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:15.120
Use the superior border of the lower rib to avoid the neurovascular structures beneath the rib above. Do not use the nipple as the sole landmark or assume every body has the same chest-wall thickness.
应靠下方肋骨上缘，避开上方肋骨下缘神经血管结构。不能只凭乳头定位，也不能认为每个人胸壁一样厚。

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:27.624
This is anatomy preparation on the approved model, not a patient puncture instruction for an unauthorized provider. Confirm the actual device, body habitus and instructor requirements.
这是批准模型上的解剖准备，不是未获准人员给患者穿刺的指示。应确认真实器械、体型及教师要求。

00:22:27.624 --> 00:22:39.240
The current PDF illustrates a BD twelve-gauge three-inch catheter and a Turkel eight-French, twelve-gauge three-and-a-half-inch assembly. They are examples with different construction.
当前PDF示出BD十二号三英寸导管，以及Turkel八法、十二号三点五英寸装置。两者结构不同，只是已标明示例。

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:53.040
The Turkel has a contact indicator and a three-way stopcock that starts closed. The BD example does not require adding a three-way stopcock. Device opening is therefore not a universal identical step.
Turkel有接触指示及起始关闭三通。BD示例不需要另加三通。因此开放器械不是所有型号都相同的一步。

00:22:53.040 --> 00:23:05.976
Do not combine the old textbook improvised glove valve, one pictured catheter and another device cap into a homemade hybrid. Follow the actual authorized assembly and its instructions.
不能把旧教材临时手套瓣膜、一个图示导管及另一个器械盖，拼成自制混合装置。应遵循真实获准装置及其说明。

00:23:05.976 --> 00:23:19.104
The school may use another training model. Recognize parts, opening state and sharps handling on that model before the supervised demonstration, rather than claiming the PDF proves school equipment identity.
学校可能使用另一训练模型。监督演示前应识别该型号部件、开放状态及锐器处理，不能称PDF证明了学校器械身份。

00:23:19.104 --> 00:23:30.744
In the supervised model sequence, first confirm the indication, role, equipment and landmark, then use the prescribed aseptic preparation and controlled handling.
在监督模型顺序中，应先确认指征、角色、器械及定位，再按规定无菌准备及受控拿持。

00:23:30.744 --> 00:23:43.920
The current procedure stops needle advancement after pleural entry, then stabilizes the assembly while the sharp is removed and the flexible catheter is advanced. Do not drive a metal needle to the hub by rote.
当前流程在进入胸膜腔后停止针前进，然后稳定装置，在移出锐针的同时推进柔性导管。不能背动作就把金属针一路推到针座。

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:55.872
Dispose of the sharp safely and open the actual device as required. A closed stopcock can prevent the intended relief; an improvised extra valve is not automatically useful.
锐针应安全丢弃，并按真实器械要求开放。关闭三通可妨碍预期减压，临时多加一个阀也不自动有益。

00:23:55.872 --> 00:24:08.712
Then reassess chest movement, air entry and hemodynamics. The observed response and ongoing patency matter more than having completed the motion or heard an initial air sound.
随后复查胸动、进气及血流动力学。观察反应及持续通畅，比完成动作或最初听见气声更重要。

00:24:08.712 --> 00:24:19.728
A catheter may not enter the pleural space or may become blocked, kinked or displaced. An initial air release is not proof of durable clinical success.
导管可能未进入胸膜腔，或发生堵塞、打折及脱位。最初出气，不证明持续临床成功。

00:24:19.728 --> 00:24:32.112
The authorized clinician must reassess the diagnosis and physiology. Mainstem intubation can produce unilateral findings, and hemorrhage or tamponade can coexist with a pneumothorax.
获准临床人员必须重评诊断及生理。主支气管插管可造成单侧发现，失血或心包填塞也可与气胸并存。

00:24:32.112 --> 00:24:47.592
An unnecessary or misplaced puncture can cause another pneumothorax, injure structures or produce bleeding or infection. The absence of absolute contraindications for a true indication does not mean every quiet chest needs a needle.
不必要或错位穿刺可造成另一个气胸、损伤结构，或引起出血及感染。真实适应证下无绝对禁忌，不代表每个安静胸部都需针刺。

00:24:47.592 --> 00:25:00.024
Repeated or alternative decompression belongs to the appropriate authorized pathway. Continue supportive care and rapid definitive transfer; a temporary catheter is not the end of the call.
重复或替代减压属于适当获准路径。应继续支持及迅速确定性转运，暂时导管不是任务终点。

00:25:00.024 --> 00:25:10.944
A hemothorax occupies pleural space and removes blood from the useful circulation. The patient can therefore have both respiratory compromise and hypovolemic shock.
血胸既占据胸膜空间，也把血从有效循环中移走，因此患者可同时有呼吸受损及低血容量休克。

00:25:10.944 --> 00:25:23.736
Blood and air may coexist. Physical signs can overlap and may be difficult to interpret in the field; do not insist on a perfect percussion result to recognize a critically injured patient.
血和气可并存，体征可能重叠，院前也可能难以判断。不能要求完美叩诊结果，才承认患者危重。

00:25:23.736 --> 00:25:35.568
A small decompression catheter intended to vent air does not solve major pleural bleeding. A chest drain and definitive surgical or other hemorrhage control are different treatments.
用于排气的细小减压导管，不能解决重要胸膜出血。胸管及确定性手术或其他止血，是不同治疗。

00:25:35.568 --> 00:25:48.240
Support breathing and perfusion, continue the search for other bleeding and arrange rapid appropriate trauma care. Report what remains uncertain rather than promising that one puncture fixed everything.
应支持呼吸及灌注，继续寻找其他出血，并迅速安排适当创伤照护。应报告仍不确定内容，不能保证一次穿刺解决一切。

00:25:48.240 --> 00:26:01.536
A flail segment can move paradoxically, but pain-related splinting or positive pressure may hide the movement. Do not require an obvious dramatic segment before addressing inadequate breathing.
连枷段可矛盾运动，但疼痛性限制或正压可能掩盖。不能等到看见夸张胸段，才处理呼吸不足。

00:26:01.536 --> 00:26:12.336
The underlying lung contusion and associated injuries can be more important than the motion itself. Respiratory function can worsen after the first examination.
深部肺挫伤及伴随伤，可能比运动本身更重要。首次检查后，呼吸功能仍可恶化。

00:26:12.336 --> 00:26:24.408
Provide indicated analgesia and oxygenation or ventilation support, with repeated assessment. Do not weigh down or circumferentially bind the chest to make the movement disappear.
应提供有指征镇痛、氧合或通气支持，并反复评估。不能压重物或环周绑胸，只为让运动消失。

00:26:24.408 --> 00:26:38.760
The examination guide mentions manual flail stabilization while Nancy rejects external stabilization. Confirm the school supervised technique and avoid inventing a restrictive compromise that impairs ventilation.
考试指南提到手动稳定连枷段，而Nancy反对外部固定。应确认学校监督技术，不能编造妨碍通气的限制性折中做法。

00:26:38.760 --> 00:26:54.216
Tamponade restricts cardiac filling within the pericardium. The classic combination of low pressure, distended veins and muffled sounds may be absent or hard to detect; equal breath sounds do not definitively identify the diagnosis.
心包填塞在心包内限制心脏充盈。低血压、静脉怒张及心音低弱的经典组合可能缺如或难测；双侧呼吸音相等，不能确定诊断。

00:26:54.216 --> 00:27:08.064
Blunt cardiac injury can cause dysrhythmia or pump dysfunction. Obtain indicated monitoring and ECG while maintaining trauma priorities, rather than interpreting a normal first tracing as structural clearance.
钝性心脏伤可造成心律失常或泵功能异常。应在维持创伤优先的同时按指征监护及采ECG，不能以首图正常排除结构伤。

00:27:08.064 --> 00:27:21.168
Major deceleration or penetration can injure the great vessels. A person can initially seem stable; pain, perfusion asymmetry and subsequent shock need appropriate trauma evaluation.
重大减速或穿透可损伤大血管，患者最初可能看似稳定。疼痛、灌注不对称及后续休克，都需要适当创伤评估。

00:27:21.168 --> 00:27:35.280
Diaphragm, esophageal and major-airway injuries can be occult or delayed. Recognize concerning patterns, support physiology and convey to definitive care without forcing a precise field diagnosis.
膈肌、食管及大气道伤可能隐匿或延迟。应识别危险模式、支持生理并送往确定性照护，不必强求精确院前诊断。

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:45.816
For the pediatric rehearsal, communicate the mechanism, new bilateral hand symptoms, actual motor and sensory findings and the movement protection used.
儿童演练中，应沟通机制、新发双手症状、真实运动及感觉发现，以及采用的移动保护。

00:27:45.816 --> 00:27:57.168
For the chest case, communicate the initial wound and the later change in breathing, asymmetry and pressure. Distinguish the suspected pressure threat from confirmed findings.
胸部案例中，应沟通初始伤口及后续呼吸、不对称和血压变化。疑似压力威胁与已确认发现应区分。

00:27:57.168 --> 00:28:10.368
Include the exact seal or supervised procedure, application time, effect and any failure or modification. A procedure name without a response does not tell the receiver what remains urgent.
应包括准确胸封或监督操作、应用时间、效果，以及失败或调整。只有操作名称而无反应，不能告诉接收方仍有什么紧急。

00:28:10.368 --> 00:28:22.632
Finish with the current patient state, support required and explicit transfer of responsibility. Do not bury a new deficit or failing chest at the end of a long list of minor injuries.
最后应说明当前状态、需要支持，并明确责任交接。不能把新神经缺损或胸部衰竭，埋在一长串轻伤最后。

00:28:22.632 --> 00:28:34.392
At the spine station, identify the correct age pathway, assess actual findings and explain the movement plan. Do not chase a negative adult rule for the symptomatic child.
脊柱站应确认正确年龄路径，评估真实发现，并解释搬运方案。不能为有症状儿童追求成人规则阴性。

00:28:34.392 --> 00:28:48.240
At the seal station, identify the real product and demonstrate its preparation, application, reassessment and failure response. State the source conflict rather than pretending it does not exist.
胸封站应识别真实产品，展示准备、应用、复评及失败处理。应说明来源冲突，不能假装不存在。

00:28:48.240 --> 00:29:01.344
At the needle trainer, state the clinical scope boundary, landmark accurately and follow the actual instructor-approved device sequence. No live-person puncture is part of this self-study rehearsal.
针刺模型站应先说明临床权限边界，准确定位，并按教师批准器械顺序。此自学演练不包括给真人穿刺。

00:29:01.344 --> 00:29:12.816
In the integrated station, a partner introduces deterioration. Repeat the primary survey, call for the appropriate support and hand over the evolving patient clearly.
整合站由搭档加入恶化变化。应重复初级评估、请求适当支持，并清楚交接变化中的患者。

00:29:12.816 --> 00:30:01.968
The literal first span finishes urinary assessment before the musculoskeletal section. Ask about voiding difficulty, pain, frequency, blood, baseline output and relevant urinary history; a bladder scan or catheterization is a separate trained/authorized task, not an automatic response to the history. Distinguish an ileal urinary conduit from a nephrostomy draining a kidney through the flank. Observe the actual stoma or insertion site, dressing, tubing and timed output without pulling, flushing or inserting into an unfamiliar system. Bowel-derived conduits can produce mucus, so appearance or smell alone neither proves infection nor makes new fever, flank pain, bleeding or a large output change normal.
字面第一段先结束泌尿评估，再进入肌骨节。应问排尿困难、疼痛、频率、血尿、平常尿量及相关病史；膀胱扫描或置管是另需训练授权的任务，不能问完病史就自动执行。须区分回肠尿路导管，以及经腰侧引流肾脏的肾造瘘。观察实际造口或入口、敷料、管路及有时间背景的尿量，不牵拉、不冲洗、不往不熟悉的系统置物。肠段导管可产黏液，因此外观气味本身既不能证明感染，也不能把新发热、腰痛、出血或尿量大变说成正常。

00:30:01.968 --> 00:30:48.168
In the musculoskeletal checklist, compare baseline mobility and permitted activity with posture, assistive devices, skin/bruising, deformity, swelling and comfortable active movement. Ask about pain, prior injury, medicines and support needs. Colour, warmth, movement and sensation, or CWMS, organize observations; normal findings do not reliably rule out every fracture, evolving compartment problem or spinal injury. Repeat the appropriate distal neurovascular findings before and after support or movement. Do not use resistance, a thirty-degree straight-leg hold or unsupported sitting to challenge a potentially unstable injured pelvis, spine or limb.
肌骨表须把基础活动和允许活动，与姿势、辅助器械、皮肤瘀伤、畸形、肿胀及舒适主动活动比较，询问痛、旧伤、药物及支持需求。颜色、温度、活动、感觉，即CWMS，用于组织观察；正常结果不能可靠排除全部骨折、演变筋膜室问题或脊柱伤。支持或移动前后重复适当远端神经血管发现。不能用抗阻、三十度直腿保持或无支持坐位，去挑战可能不稳的骨盆、脊柱或伤肢。

00:30:48.168 --> 00:31:33.192
Correct two literal assessment shortcuts. Dorsiflexion brings the front of the foot toward the shin; plantar flexion points it away. The source paragraph interchanges the resisted directions, so name and observe the actual movement rather than memorizing where its hand is written. Its zero-to-three example assesses motor block associated with epidural analgesia: zero means no motor block and three means inability to move knees or ankles. It is not a universal trauma strength score and cannot be compared directly with another scale without naming it. Weight-bearing status and a falls-risk tool guide a plan; neither a score nor willingness to walk overrides an acute injury restriction.
须纠正两项字面评估简写。背屈使前足向胫前靠近，跖屈则向远离方向指；来源抗阻方向段把二者交换，应说出并观察真实动作，不能背其写的手放位置。其零至三级例评硬膜外镇痛相关运动阻滞：零为无阻滞，三为膝踝不能动。它不是通用创伤肌力分，不能不说明量表就与其他分数直接比较。负重状态及跌倒风险工具用于规划；分数或愿意走，都不能越过急性伤情限制。

00:31:33.192 --> 00:32:27.504
The assigned mechanical-lift table distinguishes support, not interchangeable sling names. A universal sling may be fitted in a chair; the illustrated hammock gives broader head-to-knee support and cannot simply be removed with the person still seated; a hygiene sling exposes more area for toileting and gives less, short-duration support. Real compatibility, size, head control, weight capacity and training decide selection. The bed-position pages describe supine, prone, lateral, a side/semi-prone Sims posture and head-up variants. Their examples use Fowler around forty-five degrees, semi-Fowler thirty and high Fowler sixty-to-ninety. They are descriptions, not an order to roll an unstable injury, twist a neck or force every breathless/shocked patient to one angle.
指定机械吊移表区分支撑程度，不是可互换名称。通用吊带可能在椅上装入；图示吊床型从头至膝上提供较广支持，不能让人仍坐着就直接取下；卫生型为如厕暴露更多部位，支持较少且偏短时。真实相容性、尺码、头控、承重及训练决定选择。床位页描述仰、俯、侧、侧卧半俯的Sims及抬头变式；例列Fowler约45度、半Fowler30度、高Fowler60至90度。这些是描述，不命令滚动不稳伤、扭颈，或强把每个气促休克者放同一角度。

00:32:27.504 --> 00:33:24.552
At the wound-span ending, distinguish mechanism before naming a dressing. Arterial insufficiency can cause distal tissue ischemia; venous disease can produce a shallow exuding lower-leg wound with edema; neuropathy can reduce protective sensation and coexist with pressure or arterial disease. Appearances overlap, so pulse, location, pain or a textbook percentage alone cannot settle the cause. Assess circulation and the whole patient before a compression plan: a dressing for a venous-looking wound must not become unassessed tight compression over an ischemic limb. The healing figure shows overlapping clot, inflammation, new tissue and remodeling, not guaranteed strength at a calendar date. Literal reading stops at the introduction to the following healing-factor table; wider named Chapter4 teaching remains separately identified support.
伤口段末先区分机制，再谈敷料。动脉不足可致远端缺血；静脉病可有浅、渗出且伴水肿的小腿伤；神经病变可降低保护性感觉，并与压力或动脉病并存。外观有重叠，不能只靠脉搏、位置、痛或教材百分比定病因。压迫方案前须评循环和整个人，不能因像静脉伤，就未经评估紧压缺血肢。愈合图表示血块、炎症、新组织及重塑重叠，不保证某日期就够牢。字面阅读止于下一愈合因素表的介绍；较广第4章教学另作明确支持。

00:33:24.552 --> 00:34:22.752
The literal IV pages compare a short peripheral dressing with a line that also has a securement device. The shared aim is a clean, dry, inspectable site without catheter movement: identify the person/line, prepare an appropriate work area and aseptic materials, stabilize while removing the old dressing, use the actual antiseptic and allow it to dry, then apply the compatible dressing/securement and reassess. A component remaining under a central-line dressing needs the relevant sterile/no-touch handling; glove removal is not permission to touch its protected surface. Compare external length with the documented baseline: a change suggests displacement but an unchanged number does not prove internal tip position. Do not push an exposed catheter inward or improvise a central-line dressing procedure from the short-peripheral checklist.
字面静脉页比较短外周敷料与另有固定器的管路。共同目标是入口清洁干燥可观察，同时避免导管移动：确认患者和管路，备适当台面及无菌材料，去旧敷料时稳管，按真实消毒产品操作并待干，再放相容敷料固定并复评。留在中心管敷料下的部件需要相应无菌或不接触处理；摘手套不允许摸受保护面。将体外长度与记录基线比，变化提示移位，但数字未变不证明体内管尖正确。不能把露出导管推回，也不能用短外周清单临时拼中心管换药。

00:34:22.752 --> 00:35:18.960
The last literal span introduces transfusion and stops at the first three preparation steps, not a completed transfusion competency. Red cells primarily restore oxygen-carrying capacity; platelets and plasma address different hemostatic needs, and saline is not equivalent to replacing lost red cells or clotting components. Allogeneic means another donor, autologous the person's own blood. Confirm the actual authorized product, indication, identifiers, compatibility and individual consent; religion alone does not tell you which components a person accepts. Correct the source suggestion that irradiation or leukocyte reduction solves incompatibility: neither replaces compatibility testing. Irradiation inactivates donor T lymphocytes to prevent transfusion-associated graft-versus-host disease, not an ABO mismatch.
字面最后一段介绍输血，并止于准备前三步，不构成完成输血技能。红细胞主要恢复携氧能力，血小板及血浆对应不同止血需要，盐水不等于补回丢失红细胞或凝血成分。Allogeneic指其他供者，autologous指自体血。须核真实获准产品、指征、身份、相容及个人同意，不能只凭宗教推愿接受哪种成分。来源暗示辐照或去白可解决不相容，须纠正：二者都不能替代相容检验。辐照使供者T淋巴细胞失活，防输血相关移植物抗宿主病，不是修复ABO不合。

00:35:18.960 --> 00:36:10.392
The source reaction list is a warning system, not a requirement for every feature. Fever/rigors, chest or back pain, dyspnea, hives, altered pressure, dark urine or other new deterioration may matter during or after transfusion. Do not wait for a rash to cover twenty-five percent or for all vital signs to change. Canadian Blood Services advises stopping a suspected reaction and maintaining vascular access with saline under the actual response plan, then obtaining urgent clinical/transfusion-service review. The bedside task remains assessment and escalation within real training and authority, not restarting an unknown product or flushing residual blood into the patient. A new reaction and the original bleeding/illness can coexist.
来源反应清单用于警示，不要求项项都有。输血中后发热寒战、胸背痛、气促、风团、血压改变、深色尿或其他新恶化都可能重要。不能等疹覆盖百分之二十五或生命征全变。Canadian Blood Services建议疑反应时停止输注，按真实处置方案用盐水维持血管通路，再紧急请临床及输血服务评估。床边任务仍是权限训练内评估升级，不是重启未知产品或把残余血冲进患者。新反应与原失血疾病可同时存在。

00:36:10.392 --> 00:37:02.880
Explain the literal pre-transfusion preparation as a stop-before-error chain. Complete the approved preparation before obtaining a temperature-controlled product; different products have different storage requirements, so return an unusable or unneeded unit to the transfusion service rather than storing it in an ordinary refrigerator. Verify the prescribed component, amount, timing/rate and special modifications, then actual related medication orders and previous transfusion/allergy history. Do not give every patient the source example of acetaminophen, diphenhydramine or furosemide thirty minutes beforehand: premedication is individualized, not a guarantee against reactions, and can obscure symptoms. Any identity, order or product discrepancy means do not proceed until resolved.
把字面输血准备讲成防错前停链：取得控温产品前完成批准准备；不同产品储存要求不同，不能用或不再需要的单位交回输血服务，不放普通冰箱。核处方成分、数量、时点速度及特殊处理，再核相关药令、既往输血与过敏史。不能把来源对乙酰氨基酚、苯海拉明或呋塞米提前三十分钟的例子，给所有人照做：预处理需个体化，不保证无反应，还可能掩症状。身份、药令或产品有任何不符，都应先停至查清。

00:37:02.880 --> 00:37:12.936
You should be able to explain adult NEXUS and Canadian C-Spine without applying them beyond their intended pathway or using neck motion as the first examination.
你应能解释成人NEXUS及Canadian C-Spine，不超出目标路径，也不把转颈当作第一项检查。

00:37:12.936 --> 00:37:26.592
For a child with new neurological symptoms, select a protective pediatric plan and preserve breathing and perfusion. A collar is not the whole treatment and normal early bone imaging would not erase a deficit.
儿童新发神经症状时，应选择有保护性的儿童方案，并维持呼吸及灌注。颈托不是全部治疗，早期骨影像正常也不能抹去缺损。

00:37:26.592 --> 00:37:37.104
For chest trauma, explain the different mechanisms, the seal failure plan and why escalating for decompression is distinct from independent permission to perform it.
胸伤中，应解释不同机制、胸封失败预案，以及为何升级请求减压不同于获得独立实施许可。

00:37:37.104 --> 00:37:48.528
Use the two paired Nancy guides and original checks to retrieve the reasoning. The next lesson covers the assigned burns and temperature readings without mixing cooling with trauma warming.
应利用两份中英Nancy导读及原创自查，主动提取推理。下一课处理指定烧伤及温度阅读，不把降温与创伤保暖混淆。
